  "text": "To find the number of values of \\( x \\) in the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\) where \\( f(x) = \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 \\), we need to determine when the argument of the sine function equals an integer multiple of \\(\\pi\\).\n\n1. **Solve for \\(\\sin(5x)\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0\n   \\]\n   This implies:\n   \\[\n   7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x) = k\\pi \\quad \\text{for some integer } k\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\) ranges from -1 to 1, \\( k \\) must be an integer such that:\n   \\[\n   -1 \\leq \\frac{k}{7} \\leq 1 \\implies -7 \\leq k \\leq 7\n   \\]\n   Thus, \\( k \\) can take values from -7 to 7, inclusive.\n\n2. **Count the number of solutions for \\(5x\\):**\n   For each \\( k \\) in the range \\([-7, 7]\\), we solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   5x = \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right) \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 5x = \\pi - \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right)\n   \\]\n   Each of these equations will give two solutions for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( 0 < x < 2\\pi \\) because \\(\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right)\\) and \\(\\pi - \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right)\\) are symmetric about \\(\\pi/2\\).\n\n3. **Total number of solutions for \\( x \\):**\n   Since there are 15 values of \\( k \\) (from -7 to 7), and each \\( k \\) gives 2 solutions for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   n = 15 \\times 2 = 30\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the number of tangent points:**\n   The graph of \\( y = f(x) \\) is tangent to the \\( x \\)-axis at points where \\( f(x) = 0 \\). Since the sine function is periodic and symmetric, the tangent points will occur at intervals where the function changes direction smoothly.\n\n5. **Count the number of tangent points:**\n   Given the symmetry and periodicity of the sine function, each pair of solutions (one from \\(\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right)\\) and one from \\(\\pi - \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{k}{7}\\right)\\)) will have a tangent point at the midpoint of the interval between them.\n\n6. **Final count:**\n   Since each \\( k \\) pair corresponds to one tangent point, and there are 15 pairs:\n   \\[\n   t = 15\n   \\]\n\n7. **Sum \\( n + t \\):**\n   \\[\n   n + t = 30 + 15 = 45\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]",
